#: admin/help.php:49 admin/help.php:91
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:51
msgid "A Book is the landing page and table of contents for one publication. It brings together a title, an optional cover image, a subtitle, an introduction, and every Chapter assigned to it."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:52
msgid "Most day-to-day work — adding chapters, grouping them into sections, and reordering — is faster from the Make a Book admin page (Books & Chapters) than from this screen. Use this screen for the book's actual content: title, introduction, cover image, and excerpt."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:61
msgid "The Book Details panel, in the sidebar of the Book editor, controls:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:63
msgid "Subtitle — a short line shown under the book title on its landing page."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:64
msgid "Accent color — used for links, the \"Start reading\" button, and other highlights on this book's pages."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:66
msgid "These same fields are also editable from the Make a Book admin page, alongside this book's sections and chapters."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:73
msgid "Displaying Your Library"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:75
msgid "Every published book automatically appears on the library archive at /books/. To show the same library inside an existing page or post instead, add a Shortcode block containing:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:77
msgid "Add a limit=\"6\" attribute to control how many books are shown (1-100; the default is 12)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:93
msgid "A Chapter is one page of reading content that belongs to a Book. Write the chapter using normal blocks — headings, images, lists, tables, quotes, and code are all supported — the same as any other WordPress post."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:94
msgid "A chapter must be published and assigned to a Book (in the Chapter Details panel, or from the Make a Book admin page) before it appears in that book's table of contents or reading navigation."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:101
msgid "Organizing Chapters"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:103
msgid "The Chapter Details panel controls how a chapter fits into its book:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:105
msgid "Book — which book this chapter belongs to. Required."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:106
msgid "Section — an optional group, such as \"Getting Started\" or \"Part II\". Chapters assigned to the same section are grouped together, with the section's own text, in the table of contents; chapters left unassigned appear under a default \"Chapters\" heading."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:107
msgid "Chapter number / order — controls reading order, lowest to highest."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:109
msgid "Sections themselves — creating them, writing their description text, and reordering them — are managed from the Make a Book admin page (Books & Chapters), not from this screen. That page is also the fastest way to add a new chapter to a book and reorder existing ones: open a book there to see every chapter and section together in one place."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:116
msgid "Code Snippets"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help.php:118
msgid "For chapters that include code examples, search the block inserter for \"Code Snippet\" instead of using the core Code block. It adds a language label, an optional caption (e.g. a filename), and a Copy button for readers, styled to match the chapter reader."
msgstr ""

